{
  "name": "Param Template + Trim E2E (single-line string kinds)",
  "version": "1.0.0",
  "description": "An HTTP node's single-line `url` string param resolves through all three kinds plus the strict-param trim. (1) a Template-kind url `{{base_url}}/health` renders at execution (a single-line string param has a template control); (2) an Expression-kind url evaluates; (3) a literal url carrying a trailing newline is trimmed before the request (strict single-line trim). A POST with a multiline Template body proves the re-homed multiline body template still renders after the StringInput unification. Each request's final_url / echoed body is bound to a variable and read back by a downstream Log so the run output asserts the resolved value.",
